WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:04.400
-Donald Trump made an appearance
on Fox News last night,

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.234
and he was very normal
and coherent

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:09.434
and made lots of lucid,
intelligent comments and...

00:00:09.434 --> 00:00:11.434
Sorry.
It just seems a little weird.

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:14.267
Are you sure that card
is right, Wally?

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:15.968
-Sorry, Seth.
I just hired a new guy.

00:00:15.968 --> 00:00:17.367
Let me make sure
there aren't any mistakes.

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:18.367
-Okay.

00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:21.701
Should just be a second,
everybody.

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:23.868
[ Pen scribbling ]
-Oh. That's spelled wrong.

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:25.167
That too.

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:27.667
Oh, boy, he messed that part up
really bad.

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:29.734
I don't even know
what he was trying to do there.

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:32.367
Okay, just the one final change,
and we're good.

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:33.767
Okay, Seth. All set.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:36.000
-Alright. Okay, great.
Here we go.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.767
Donald Trump went
on Fox News last night

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:39.100
and lost his [bleep] mind.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.334
Alright. Thanks, Wally.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:42.667
-No worries, boss.
-Okay.

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:43.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.834 --> 00:00:45.834
Hey, who is, uh...

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:47.667
Who is this new guy, by the way?

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:50.167
-Eh, just some kid I met on one
of those QAnon message boards.

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:51.701
You'd like him.
-Oh, I bet I would.

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:54.033
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:56.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:57.968
♪♪

00:00:57.968 --> 00:01:00.367
Okay, so, you know
how Donald Trump is still,

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:02.534
as of this moment, the leader
of the Republican Party

00:01:02.534 --> 00:01:05.968
and front-runner for the party's
presidential nomination in 2024?

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:09.033
And you know how he's also
what constitutional scholars

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:11.033
technically refer to
as a, quote,

00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:12.501
"ass-load of legal trouble"?

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:14.767
Well, yesterday
he went on Fox News

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:16.100
to talk about all of it.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.534
And as is par for the course
for Trump, despite being

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:20.667
sort of softball question
after softball question,

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:22.701
he fully disintegrated
into a sweaty,

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:24.534
red-faced, rambling,
incoherent mess.

00:01:24.534 --> 00:01:27.367
It's amazing that Trump
continues to have the confidence

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:29.200
of a man
who is ready for anything

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.868
while being prepared
for nothing.

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:31.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:33.300
If Trump was on "Family Feud,"

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:36.634
he would buzz in before
he got asked a question.

00:01:36.634 --> 00:01:38.133
"Top five answers on the board."

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:39.400
[ Bell dings ]

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.400
[ As Trump ]
"Hunter Biden's laptop."

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:44.868
[ Normal voice ]
"Well, the question was gonna be

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:46.367
best places for a first date,

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:47.701
so I don't think
it's gonna be up there."

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:49.200
[ As Trump ]
"Well, it's got to be somewhere.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.701
We might as well look there."

00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:52.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:53.400
[ Normal voice ]
Now, we all know

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.133
that whenever he goes
on Fox News

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:57.000
or does a rally or speaks
in public in any way,

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.801
Trump is gonna say
a bunch of crazy [bleep]

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:00.501
But that's especially
problematic right now

00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:02.267
because he's facing multiple,

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:04.868
very serious criminal
investigations and civil suits

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:07.334
and what he says can be used
against him in court.

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:09.934
There are multiple grand juries
looking into his attempts

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:11.334
to overturn the 2020 election.

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:13.701
There's the Justice
Department's investigation

00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:16.167
of all the classified documents
he stole from the White House.

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:19.100
And there's the lawsuit
New York Attorney General

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:20.868
Letitia James
announced yesterday,

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:23.667
seeking to bar him
from doing business in the state

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:26.934
after what she called years
of staggering fraud.

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:28.901
-The New York state
attorney general suing

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:31.334
former President Trump,
three of his adult children,

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:34.834
and the Trump Organization
for $250 million,

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:36.501
accusing the Trump family
of, quote,

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:39.234
"staggering fraud"
in a sweeping civil suit

00:02:39.234 --> 00:02:41.901
and looking to ban them from
doing business in New York.

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:46.868
-We show that they violated
several state criminal laws,

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:51.234
including falsifying
business records,

00:02:51.234 --> 00:02:54.667
issuing false
financial statements,

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:58.868
insurance fraud,
and engaging in a conspiracy

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:05.267
to commit each of these
state law violations.

00:03:05.267 --> 00:03:07.701
We believe the conduct
alleged in this action

00:03:07.701 --> 00:03:10.634
also violates
federal criminal law,

00:03:10.634 --> 00:03:13.300
including issuing
false statements

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:17.167
to financial institutions,
and bank fraud.

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:19.734
-At this point, it would just
be easier to list the crimes

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:21.400
Trump hasn't committed.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.801
I mean, as far as we know,

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:24.634
he hasn't broken
any maritime laws.

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:26.534
Although we say that now,
and then like in a week,

00:03:26.534 --> 00:03:27.868
audio will surface of Trump

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:30.868
trying to bribe a seal to prove
the election was stolen.

00:03:30.868 --> 00:03:32.934
[ As Trump ]
Bark bark, clap clap, bark,

00:03:32.934 --> 00:03:36.100
Dominion voting machines --
excuse me! -- clap, bark.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:39.067
[ Normal voice ] He also
probably hasn't jaywalked,

00:03:39.067 --> 00:03:41.367
but only because jaywalking
happens in a straight line

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:43.400
and Trump only goes
around in circles.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:48.767
It's also very funny that James
is suing Trump for $250 million,

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:51.701
an amount he would definitely
never be able to pay.

00:03:51.701 --> 00:03:53.467
If the suit succeeds,
we're gonna see

00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:55.701
an "everything must go" sign
on Trump Tower.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:58.868
It would be
the tackiest fire sale ever.

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:00.601
You'd just see a bunch
of New Yorkers

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:02.167
walking down Fifth Avenue

00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:04.000
lugging giant chandeliers

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.033
or marble water fountains
or a golden toilet.

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:08.968
"Can you believe it?
I got this for 20 bucks.

00:04:08.968 --> 00:04:10.467
If the Yankees
win the World Series,

00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:13.067
I'm gonna get wasted
and puke in this thing!"

00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:14.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:17.067
"I'm gonna puke like a king."

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:19.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.834 --> 00:04:22.067
And then there's
the DOJ investigation

00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:23.400
of the classified documents.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.968
Yesterday, we told you that
the independent arbiter

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:28.534
who had been appointed to sift
through the material seized

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:32.067
in the FBI search of Mar-a-Lago
had chastised

00:04:32.067 --> 00:04:34.367
the Trump legal team
for not providing any proof

00:04:34.367 --> 00:04:36.501
that Trump had declassified
any of the documents.

00:04:36.501 --> 00:04:39.000
And sure enough, yesterday,
an appeals court intervened

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.501
to reverse a lower court ruling

00:04:40.501 --> 00:04:43.133
and allow the DOJ investigation
to continue.

00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:45.133
The appeals court judges
ruled that

00:04:45.133 --> 00:04:47.467
the DOJ could move forward
with its criminal investigation

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:49.467
because there's no reason
to believe

00:04:49.467 --> 00:04:51.100
Trump declassified the documents

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:54.234
or that he should get
to keep them even if he did.

00:04:54.234 --> 00:04:55.400
-Just a short time ago,

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.400
the 11th Circuit
Court of Appeals

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.534
handed Trump's lawyers
a huge defeat.

00:05:00.534 --> 00:05:02.067
Three appeals court judges,

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:04.567
two of them appointed
by Trump himself,

00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:06.801
lifted a judge's order
that prevented

00:05:06.801 --> 00:05:09.701
the Justice Department
from using classified documents

00:05:09.701 --> 00:05:12.968
that were seized from Mar-a-Lago
in its criminal investigation.

00:05:12.968 --> 00:05:15.534
-An appeals court has ruled
that the Justice Department

00:05:15.534 --> 00:05:19.000
can have access to roughly 100
highly sensitive

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:22.000
classified documents
that were taken from Mar-a-Lago.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.534
Trump has been arguing
that all the documents

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:27.334
seized from his club
are his personal property

00:05:27.334 --> 00:05:29.934
and that if the FBI found
anything classified in there,

00:05:29.934 --> 00:05:31.267
well, Trump magically

00:05:31.267 --> 00:05:32.968
declassified it
when he was president,

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:35.834
even though he has no record
of ever having done that.

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:37.200
The judges write, quote,

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.901
"The declassification argument
is a red herring

00:05:39.901 --> 00:05:41.801
because declassifying
an official document

00:05:41.801 --> 00:05:44.667
would not change its content
or render it personal.

00:05:44.667 --> 00:05:47.534
So even if we assumed
that Plaintiff, Trump,

00:05:47.534 --> 00:05:50.167
did declassify some
or all of these documents,

00:05:50.167 --> 00:05:53.133
that would not explain why he
has a personal interest in them.

00:05:53.133 --> 00:05:55.200
-Exactly.
Claiming you declassified them,

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.234
on top of being a lie,
is also irrelevant.

00:05:57.234 --> 00:05:58.701
You don't get to keep them.

00:05:58.701 --> 00:06:01.467
Trump thinks declassifying
something is like calling dibs.

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:04.334
Watch out if you're ever
at a big group dinner with him.

00:06:04.334 --> 00:06:06.334
[ As Trump ]
I'm officially declassifying

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:08.000
those jalapeno poppers.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.334
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:10.734
So hands off the poppers.

00:06:10.734 --> 00:06:13.033
But also, before
I declassify the poppers,

00:06:13.033 --> 00:06:14.467
we ordered the poppers
as a group,

00:06:14.467 --> 00:06:18.634
so we'll still be splitting
the check for the poppers.

00:06:18.634 --> 00:06:20.334
You pay for my pop.

00:06:20.334 --> 00:06:21.667
[ Laughter ]

00:06:21.667 --> 00:06:24.000
You pay, my pop.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.634
[ Normal voice ]
So, that's what was happening

00:06:25.634 --> 00:06:27.734
as Trump sat down
with his best friend

00:06:27.734 --> 00:06:30.067
slash only friend,
Sean Hannity.

00:06:30.067 --> 00:06:32.067
And as is usual --

00:06:32.067 --> 00:06:33.934
as is usually the case
with these interviews,

00:06:33.934 --> 00:06:36.167
Hannity desperately tried
to help Trump out

00:06:36.167 --> 00:06:38.200
by teeing him up
with softball questions

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:40.834
designed to defend Trump,
but accidentally ended up giving

00:06:40.834 --> 00:06:43.667
Trump free rein to go totally
off script and screw himself.

00:06:43.667 --> 00:06:45.133
For example,
as we mentioned earlier,

00:06:45.133 --> 00:06:47.834
Trump and his lawyers have been
arguing that he declassified

00:06:47.834 --> 00:06:49.300
the documents
he stole from the White House.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.100
So far, they have refused
to provide any details

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:55.801
or evidence as to how
and when exactly that happened.

00:06:55.801 --> 00:06:57.968
And now we know why --
there are none.

00:06:57.968 --> 00:06:59.434
Trump told Hannity

00:06:59.434 --> 00:07:02.567
he thinks you can declassify
a top secret document by simply

00:07:02.567 --> 00:07:04.601
declaring it declassified

00:07:04.601 --> 00:07:06.934
inside your own head.

00:07:06.934 --> 00:07:09.267
-You had said on Truth Social
a number of times

00:07:09.267 --> 00:07:10.467
you did declassify.

00:07:10.467 --> 00:07:11.901
-I did declassify. Yes.
-Okay.

00:07:11.901 --> 00:07:13.434
Well, is there a process?

00:07:13.434 --> 00:07:14.934
What was your process
to declassify?

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:17.901
-There doesn't have to be
a process, as I understand it.

00:07:17.901 --> 00:07:19.634
You know, there's different --
people say different things,

00:07:19.634 --> 00:07:21.267
but as I understand it,
there doesn't have to be...

00:07:21.267 --> 00:07:22.968
If you're the president
of the United States,

00:07:22.968 --> 00:07:26.000
you can declassify just
by saying it's declassified,

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.801
even by thinking about it.

00:07:27.801 --> 00:07:29.801
[ Laughter ]

00:07:29.801 --> 00:07:32.801
-Do you think the whole time
Trump was answering,

00:07:32.801 --> 00:07:34.133
Hannity was thinking,

00:07:34.133 --> 00:07:37.467
"Why the [bleep] did I ask him
what his process was?

00:07:37.467 --> 00:07:39.434
Ohh, what the [bleep]
is wrong with me?!

00:07:39.434 --> 00:07:42.767
Oh, today's the day
he's gonna have a process.

00:07:42.767 --> 00:07:45.167
Get your head out of your ass,
Hannity!"

00:07:45.167 --> 00:07:46.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:46.834 --> 00:07:48.601
Trump's argument
is that you can just

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:50.367
declassify things in your mind.

00:07:50.367 --> 00:07:53.400
It's officially declassified

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:56.734
as long as you believe
it's declassified.

00:07:56.734 --> 00:07:59.167
That's according to Trump's
newest legal adviser,

00:07:59.167 --> 00:08:00.234
Tinkerbell.

00:08:00.234 --> 00:08:02.133
Oh, and heads up...

00:08:02.133 --> 00:08:03.300
Heads up, Tink --

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.634
he's not gonna pay you.

00:08:05.634 --> 00:08:07.467
So, Trump says you can
declassify something

00:08:07.467 --> 00:08:08.534
just by thinking about it.

00:08:08.534 --> 00:08:10.167
Although even that
is a shaky defense

00:08:10.167 --> 00:08:11.934
because it requires
establishing that Trump

00:08:11.934 --> 00:08:14.167
is capable of thinking
about things.

00:08:14.167 --> 00:08:17.067
I mean, even if it were true

00:08:17.067 --> 00:08:18.667
that the law said you could
declassify something

00:08:18.667 --> 00:08:20.834
just by thinking about it,
all a judge would have to do

00:08:20.834 --> 00:08:24.400
is look into Trump's eyes
and immediately rule

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.734
that there's just nothing
going on in there.

00:08:26.734 --> 00:08:28.067
[ Laughter ]

00:08:28.067 --> 00:08:29.968
I mean, look at that.
Does that look more like a man

00:08:29.968 --> 00:08:32.701
who is declassifying
top secret documents

00:08:32.701 --> 00:08:35.701
or an emu who just found
the zoo camera?

00:08:35.701 --> 00:08:37.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:42.367
Whenever he's on TV,
Trump has this energy.

00:08:42.367 --> 00:08:43.801
-It's amazing to me --

00:08:43.801 --> 00:08:45.501
Emmanuel, don't do it.
Emmanuel.

00:08:45.501 --> 00:08:47.000
Emmanuel.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.834
I'm trying to tell them
thank you.

00:08:48.834 --> 00:08:50.167
Buddy, I'm trying to tell them
thank you.

00:08:50.167 --> 00:08:51.200
Don't do it. Don't.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:52.701
Emmanuel.

00:08:52.701 --> 00:08:54.701
Emmanuel. Emmanuel.

00:08:54.701 --> 00:08:55.901
Emmanuel...

00:08:55.901 --> 00:08:57.901
-Interestingly, Emmanuel

00:08:57.901 --> 00:09:00.167
also stole a bunch
of classified documents.

00:09:00.167 --> 00:09:01.267
[ Laughter ]

00:09:01.267 --> 00:09:02.767
There was also
this part of the clip

00:09:02.767 --> 00:09:04.200
that I thought
was very revealing

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:06.801
and probably drove
Trump's lawyers insane.

00:09:06.801 --> 00:09:08.133
-Is there a process?

00:09:08.133 --> 00:09:09.634
What was your process
to declassify?

00:09:09.634 --> 00:09:12.534
-There doesn't have to be
a process, as I understand it.

00:09:12.534 --> 00:09:14.334
You know, there's different --
people say different things,

00:09:14.334 --> 00:09:15.934
but as I understand it,
there doesn't have to be...

00:09:15.934 --> 00:09:18.067
There doesn't have to be
a process.

00:09:18.067 --> 00:09:20.567
There can be a process,
but there doesn't have to be.

00:09:20.567 --> 00:09:23.601
-What do you mean there doesn't
have to be a process?

00:09:23.601 --> 00:09:25.934
If Trump had been one of
the framers of the Constitution,

00:09:25.934 --> 00:09:28.534
every article would have
ended with "or not!"

00:09:28.534 --> 00:09:29.534
[ Laughter ]

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:35.968
Of course, there is a process.
It's government.

00:09:35.968 --> 00:09:37.133
There's a process
for everything.

00:09:37.133 --> 00:09:38.200
Nothing happens by magic.

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:39.534
You can't just change
your address

00:09:39.534 --> 00:09:41.667
or file your taxes
by thinking about it.

00:09:41.667 --> 00:09:44.334
Although based on Letitia James'
press conference,

00:09:44.334 --> 00:09:47.133
that's what Trump will probably
use as his next excuse.

00:09:47.133 --> 00:09:49.467
[ As Trump ] I may have inflated
my assets on legal bank forms,

00:09:49.467 --> 00:09:53.000
but in my head I was honest
down to the last penny.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:54.834
[ Normal voice ] But by far the
craziest part of the interview

00:09:54.834 --> 00:09:57.667
came when Trump fully unraveled
and seemed to suggest

00:09:57.667 --> 00:10:00.167
that the FBI was maybe
searching Mar-a-Lago

00:10:00.167 --> 00:10:03.100
to look for
Hillary Clinton's emails.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:05.200
It made so little sense,
even Hannity

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:06.868
had to jump in and stop him.

00:10:06.868 --> 00:10:09.033
-There's also a lot
of speculation

00:10:09.033 --> 00:10:10.400
because of what they did,

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:14.534
the severity of the FBI coming
and raiding Mar-a-Lago --

00:10:14.534 --> 00:10:16.701
were they looking for
the Hillary Clinton emails

00:10:16.701 --> 00:10:19.434
that were deleted,
but they are around someplace.

00:10:19.434 --> 00:10:21.067
Were they looking for the --
spying on Trump's --

00:10:21.067 --> 00:10:22.567
-Wait, you're not saying
you had it, did...?

00:10:22.567 --> 00:10:24.067
-No, no.
They may be saying...

00:10:24.067 --> 00:10:26.567
They may have thought
that it was in there.

00:10:26.567 --> 00:10:27.901
-Wait, what? The...

00:10:27.901 --> 00:10:29.167
[ Laughter ]

00:10:29.167 --> 00:10:32.501
The FBI searched
your private resort

00:10:32.501 --> 00:10:33.901
to look for
Hillary Clinton's emails?

00:10:33.901 --> 00:10:37.067
The ones you supposedly
been looking for forever.

00:10:37.067 --> 00:10:38.267
That made so little sense,

00:10:38.267 --> 00:10:39.834
even Hannity had to jump in
and say...

00:10:39.834 --> 00:10:41.267
-Don't do it.

00:10:41.267 --> 00:10:42.400
[ Laughter ]

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:43.934
-But, man, what a twist --
It would be...

00:10:43.934 --> 00:10:45.167
What a twist it would be

00:10:45.167 --> 00:10:47.000
if Trump accidentally admitted
that he's the one

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.434
who stole all of Hillary
Clinton's missing emails.

00:10:49.434 --> 00:10:51.601
I mean, honestly,
that would be worth it.

00:10:51.601 --> 00:10:53.167
Even M. Night Shyamalan
would have been like,

00:10:53.167 --> 00:10:55.367
"[Bleep] Hats off. I mean..."

00:10:55.367 --> 00:10:56.701
[ As Trump ]
A lot of people are saying

00:10:56.701 --> 00:10:58.801
maybe the FBI was looking
for Hillary's emails

00:10:58.801 --> 00:11:01.467
because maybe they were in there
because maybe in 2015

00:11:01.467 --> 00:11:03.567
I sat down at a computer
and broke into a server

00:11:03.567 --> 00:11:06.000
and stole them,
because in reality,

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.901
despite representing
as a very dumb man,

00:11:07.901 --> 00:11:10.300
I'm actually a computer genius.

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:11.801
A hacker!

00:11:11.801 --> 00:11:13.801
[ Laughter ]

00:11:15.467 --> 00:11:17.200
That's what we call ourselves.

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:19.400
We love the hackers, don't we?

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:20.868
[ Laughter ]

00:11:20.868 --> 00:11:23.434
[ Normal voice ] This guy
is still, as of this moment,

00:11:23.434 --> 00:11:24.868
the leader of
the Republican Party

00:11:24.868 --> 00:11:27.501
and the front-runner for their
presidential nomination in 2024.

00:11:27.501 --> 00:11:28.767
There are pro-Trump candidates

00:11:28.767 --> 00:11:30.534
up and down the ballot
across the country,

00:11:30.534 --> 00:11:31.868
and this is what
they're standing behind.

00:11:31.868 --> 00:11:33.200
The guy is so corrupt

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:35.934
that at this point
he can commit crimes just...

00:11:35.934 --> 00:11:37.267
-By thinking about it.

00:11:37.267 --> 00:11:39.934
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:39.934 --> 00:11:43.501
♪♪

